{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188686-let-s-fix-the-disparates","id":1188686,"title":"Let's Fix the Disparates","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-22T15:54:14-08:00","id":1188686,"title":"Let's Fix the Disparates","content":"So, let's talk about the Disparates.<br /> <br /> Everybody seems to like the Crafts that comprise them (Except the Hollowers, but I've said enough about them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). But the Disparate Alliance itself, the organization introduced in M20, has been pretty universally panned. I have genuinely not met a single person that thought they were anything better than merely usable.<br /> <br /> I don't necessarily disagree with that, but I'd like to get peoples opinions on it. What doesn't work about the concept? What, if anything, is salvageable about the idea?<br /> <br /> For my money, the issues are twofold:<br /> <br /> 1) They are a bunch of deliberately isolated, insular organizations, many of them with pretty radical ideologies, without even the the vague connective tissues that the Traditions have. There is no paradigmatic or ideological overlap between any of them. They lack even the Traditions laissez faire &quot;I respect and fight for your right to have your own paradigm, even if it's different from mine&quot; angle. There is <i>no reason </i>for them not to hate eachother, except that they hate the Technocracy more. And for some of them, not even that makes a whole lot of sense *cough*Wu Lung*cough*<br /> <br /> 2) The way they're presented. This is the one that <i>really </i>bugs me. M20 bends over backwards to present the Disparates as the &quot;one true protagonist faction&quot;. The Traditions are incompetent, the Technocrats are corrupted by Nephandi, they are the <i>only </i>good guys and the only ones that can really fight the looming Nephandic threat. It takes three editions, twenty years and an entire fandom's worth of character development (for lack of a better term) and undoes it to portray this ill conceived group as &quot;the Traditions, but better&quot;.<br /> <br /> At least, that's my take on it.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T16:14:25-08:00","id":1188694,"title":"","content":"It feels to me quite simply if a Templar can get along with a Wu Lung he sure as hell should be able to get along with a Celestial Choruster. Now not wanting to be the Low people on the totem pole I can see. The Fix I try to use is the Disparate Alliance is kind of like the Free Council in New Mage. They are in &quot;Alliance&quot; with the Traditions, they will generally work together if the Technos get assholish in the area but neither side generally has any say on the other.<br /> <br /> The Batini want to make one big super group, but baby steps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T16:58:52-08:00","id":1188706,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t see the disparate alliance as a formal order of rule like the traditions. Rather I just see it as members from various crafts that realise they are horribly outnumbered and attacked on all sides<br /> <br /> They don\u2019t meet together in meetings and have organised hierarchies, but rather acknowledge that, as a fringe member of Mage society, no one else is going to stick up for them anymore. I see the group as being made up of a very small number of members from each craft. They meet in secret and perhaps don\u2019t even know all the members of the alliance. Not even the members of the crafts are fully aware of who is and isn\u2019t in the alliance. And indeed I\u2019d say that those higher up the chain of command within the crafts may actually be deftly against any kind of alliance of the sort. The seneshels of the Tenplars would scoff at the idea working with an Islamic heathen, but perhaps one of the bit perhaps one of the brothers considers the way of god to be more than what their commanders tell them, and that their mission first and foremost is to protect the weak, and a batini in need is worthy as anyone else.<br /> I can imagine a batini who is tired of hiding in the shadows, a Templar who is fed up of seeing everyone as a potential enemy, and a Hollower who just can\u2019t stand how defeatest certain members of what can laughably be called his peers are being in the face of all this war, they meet like any other cabal meets, and soon word spreads, rippling through the underground. A resistance is forming, and as the ascension war starts to rage on for round two, these few bond together as outcasts.<br /> <br /> The one thing that unites them all is persecution. Whether the wu leng by the Akashics, or the Templars by the Order of Reason. They have all suffered at the hands of the major players of the ascension war, and always desperately and alone.<br /> <br /> Unlike the traditions, their numbers are few. They have lost members to the traditions in the wake of the reckoning, and know that those who still stand independent of the traditions will soon be lost to the world.<br /> <br /> If the technocracy were 10,000 people, and the traditions 1,000. Then the crafts would be 100, and the disparates only 10.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T18:26:08-08:00","id":1188731,"title":"","content":"The way how I see the Disparate Alliance is thus:<br /> <br /> A very, VERY reluctant alliance made out of need then of want.<br /> <br /> That if it was up to either of the individual Disparates, they wouldn't have agreed to it to begin with. But because of the omnipresence of the Technocracy and Nephandi influence, their hand is being forced.<br /> <br /> However, on a day-to-day level, they mostly stay out of each other's way and go about their business as normal. That the only thing that would be frowned upon are openly violent and hostile confrontations with each other...otherwise that's it. But when shit goes down and they uncover the latest Technocracy plot that could make a big hit to other mages in the area, and they know for sure that the resources of one Disparate won't be enough to deal with it? Sure, they'll team up to take care of the issue. &quot;Enemy of my enemy&quot; and all that. After that's been sorted out, the Disparates involved break off, go their separate ways, and go back to whatever they were doing.<br /> <br /> So kind of like Netflix Defenders: very individualistic groups that like being left alone, but only coming together when the need arises.<br /> <br /> Seems workable to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T18:33:07-08:00","id":1188735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188686-let-s-fix-the-disparates?p=1188731#post1188731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way how I see the Disparate Alliance is thus:<br /> <br /> A very, VERY reluctant alliance made out of need then of want.<br /> <br /> That if it was up to either of the individual Disparates, they wouldn't have agreed to it to begin with. But because of the omnipresence of the Technocracy and Nephandi influence, their hand is being forced.<br /> <br /> However, on a day-to-day level, they mostly stay out of each other's way and go about their business as normal. That the only thing that would be frowned upon are openly violent and hostile confrontations with each other...otherwise that's it. But when shit goes down and they uncover the latest Technocracy plot that could make a big hit to other mages in the area, and they know for sure that the resources of one Disparate won't be enough to deal with it? Sure, they'll team up to take care of the issue. &quot;Enemy of my enemy&quot; and all that. After that's been sorted out, the Disparates involved break off, go their separate ways, and go back to whatever they were doing.<br /> <br /> So kind of like Netflix Defenders: very individualistic groups that like being left alone, but only coming together when the need arises.<br /> <br /> Seems workable to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> IT seems like when the Technocracy is quite possibly at its weakest and least likely to be pushing Pogroms this set up seems rather odd, and there's the whole &quot;well why not work with the Traditions every so often&quot; then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T20:05:02-08:00","id":1188757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188686-let-s-fix-the-disparates?p=1188706#post1188706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t see the disparate alliance as a formal order of rule like the traditions. Rather I just see it as members from various crafts that realise they are horribly outnumbered and attacked on all sides<br /> <br /> Unlike the traditions, their numbers are few. They have lost members to the traditions in the wake of the reckoning, and know that those who still stand independent of the traditions will soon be lost to the world.<br /> <br /> If the technocracy were 10,000 people, and the traditions 1,000. Then the crafts would be 100, and the disparates only 10.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't depend on the craft? The Batini should be quite large I think. They were a full sized tradition. They left of their own accord and their specialty is hididng so they shouldn't have taken much damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T20:05:15-08:00","id":1188758,"title":"","content":"The question I have is why the early Revised-era Technocracy <i>did</i> push Pogroms against the Crafts. Answer that, and the rest becomes much more believable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T21:10:11-08:00","id":1188772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188686-let-s-fix-the-disparates?p=1188731#post1188731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way how I see the Disparate Alliance is thus:<br /> <br /> A very, VERY reluctant alliance made out of need then of want.<br /> <br /> That if it was up to either of the individual Disparates, they wouldn't have agreed to it to begin with. But because of the omnipresence of the Technocracy and Nephandi influence, their hand is being forced.<br /> <br /> However, on a day-to-day level, they mostly stay out of each other's way and go about their business as normal. That the only thing that would be frowned upon are openly violent and hostile confrontations with each other...otherwise that's it. But when shit goes down and they uncover the latest Technocracy plot that could make a big hit to other mages in the area, and they know for sure that the resources of one Disparate won't be enough to deal with it? Sure, they'll team up to take care of the issue. &quot;Enemy of my enemy&quot; and all that. After that's been sorted out, the Disparates involved break off, go their separate ways, and go back to whatever they were doing.<br /> <br /> So kind of like Netflix Defenders: very individualistic groups that like being left alone, but only coming together when the need arises.<br /> <br /> Seems workable to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>More or less how I see it.<br /> <br /> They aren't doing much things together. The less antagonistic crafts give each-other berth and it's a sorta truce for the more antagonistic ones. Although, when shit hits the fan, they'd be more likely to call each other, rather than the Traditions which screwed them many times already. I also think it works more on the local level than anything bigger. Sure, the Battini want more, but I don't think what they want is feasible, at least not in the foreseeable future.<br /> <br /> It's a bit like how alliances were formed between nations, which were warred with each-other for centuries, when they absolutely has to do it, because of an external threat. The Holy League, for example, or any of the World Wars.<br /> <br /> Also, a thing I'm not sure: are they even a thing outside the US? I don't want to be cynical and say that their existence is more-or-less because of the writer's view on US minority politics and that is why it feels quite straining and forced, buuuuuut...<br /> <br /> Regardless, I still think it could work. There are some parts about them in the Book of Shadows I didn't read them, so I don't know how much fleshing-out they got. Ultimately, as above, I can imagine it as a very-<i>very</i> loose alliance, than any kind of &quot;real&quot; organization.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T22:02:13-08:00","id":1188777,"title":"","content":"Let's put it this way: why should we call foul on the Disparate Alliance being unlikely now, yet the Council of Nine Mystic Traditions is given a free pass?<br /> <br /> That's basically what the Disparate Alliance IS. It's the Traditions, but started later, and with different fellowships forming the starting roster. And if we look back at Mage lore, the Tradition Council was as insane an idea back in the middle ages as the Disparate Alliance is now. More insane, actually, because at least the modern era has spread ideas of tolerance. Most of the Craft mages in the Disparate Alliance were born into cultures that tried to teach people the concept of not being hostile to folks who are culturally different (even if that idea isn't always followed or given more than lip service). In the Dark Ages, a person not having the exact same world view as you might as well have been an alien, and needed to be viewed with hostility and suspicion.<br /> <br /> Do you really think the initial interactions between the Batini and the Celestial Chorus were qualitatively different or less strained than the interactions between the Batini and the Templars? Do you think the Wu Lung condescending to literally every other group is much different than what the Order of Hermes was doing back in the day?<br /> <br /> Yes, the Disparate Alliance is, charitably, a powder keg waiting to go off. Yes, it's trying to get a dozen radically different groups to work together, when their world views are often mutually exclusive. That's not a bug, but a feature. This marriage of convenience and necessity creates drama, and room for stories. Which, as we should all know, is the whole point of the exercise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T22:12:54-08:00","id":1188778,"title":"","content":"OTOH, what do they bring to the table that the Traditions don't already bring? <br /> <br /> My problem with the Disparates isn't that they're unworkable; it's that they're redundant: the Traditions have already done the \u201cwildly diverse magical societies find common ground and forge a lasting partnership\u201d thing. I don't see anything that the Disparate Alliance offers that the Traditions don't already cover, and better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-23-2018, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T22:24:09-08:00","id":1188780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188686-let-s-fix-the-disparates?p=1188778#post1188778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OTOH, what do they bring to the table that the Traditions don't already bring?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nothing. That's the problem. Besides having different members, less structure than the Traditions, and not being obsessed with the number 9, the two organizations serve the same narrative purpose and have the same goals.<br /> <br /> Stop the Technocracy. Stop the Nephandi. Survive.<br /> <br /> Hell, since the Avatar Storm removed most of the Tradition's leadership, the Disparates can't even claim to be the one faction that let's the new blood have influence and break tradition. So what's their point? Besides, being vaguely better than the Tradition and making the Crafts relevant I can't tell.<br /> <br /> To be honest, the entire metaplot surrounding the Alliance, with the Technocracy being taken over the Nephandi kind of annoys me, since I thought that was just a lazy way of making the Technocrats EVIL again.<br /> <br /> That said, if I wanted to fix them I'd just make them a somewhat large Cabal of outcasts from various Crafts who've decided that the Technocracy (which has no real problem with Nephandi corruption) must be destroyed by any means necessary. Basically, while the Traditions are rebuilding and reexamining itself after the Avatar Storm, these guys are trying to bring back the Ascension War. Consequences be damned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1675,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","user":"Weirdboyz","date":". 02-23-2018, 01:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T23:02:22-08:00","id":1188786,"title":"","content":"I can think of three things that the Disparates do that the Traditions don't.<br /> <br /> 1) They are a <i>unique</i> combination of mismatched cultural groups. While the broad strokes run parallel to the Traditions, the devil is in the details. Different stories can be told with them, because the particular needs of the Crafts, and how they grind against each other, are not the same as those of the Traditions. Even in those instances when certain Crafts and Traditions are rough counterparts to one another. While the Wu Lung and Order of Hermes are both big into High Ritual Magick, their approaches to it, and their outlooks and attitudes, are far different, leading to different outcomes when those groups deal with other members of their respective sects.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2) As an adjunct to the above, the Disparates have a major difference from the Traditions: there are fewer White European groups in the Disparates. While the Traditions were multicultural, that sect had a large number of member groups that came from Europe or the West. Order of Hermes, Celestial Chorus, Verbana, Solificati, and multiple subsections of other Traditions. This European influence had major effects on how the Traditions were formed, developed, and operated. The Disparate Alliance, meanwhile, has a less prominent presence of White European culture, and a greater concentration of groups culled from non-White, non-European peoples and ideologies. Probably the single biggest Craft in the Alliance is the Bata'a, a group of Vodoun practitioners with a long history of problems with Whitey. For better or worse, this difference in race/culture representation DOES affect what kind of stories can be told with the Disparate Alliance.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3) Most importantly, the Disparate Alliance isn't just the Traditions. It's the Traditions AS FORMED IN MODERN DAY. The Council of Nine Mystic Traditions is a sect that is, by this point, Old. It's been around a while, and thus its members have figured out how to be in a combined sect about as well as they ever will. Inter-Tradition relations are hardly perfect, but the centuries these groups have worked together have made them familiar. They are comfortable in their place in the world, to a certain extent. The Traditions ARE.<br /> <br /> The Disparate Alliance, however, is New. It's untested, half-formed, and tenuous. The Disparate Alliance has a place in the game because it stands in contrast to the Traditions. It can go places the Traditions can't, because the latter is an established confederation. All this, while the two groups exist concurrently. You might be able to run a Traditions game where the sect is new...but you'd do it back in the Renaissance, which radically alters what kind of game you'd be playing. The Disparate Alliance allows one to run all the drama and story possibility that comes with a new, untested sect, while also having it play out in contemporary times.<br /> <br /> How do you think the idea of a First Cabal would play out in an era where modern telecommunications technology exists? How do you USE the fact that this new Mystic sect isn't the only major one in the Ascension War? Or hell, how much more interesting could it be for said Ascension War to have three big sides, rather than two? (Yes, the Nephandi and Marauders also exist, but they're smaller than the others, and have goals and methods that make them exceptions). How much more drama can arise when the technomancers in the Traditions are the only ones who could potentially be spies for a rival sect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 02-23-2018, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T00:42:32-08:00","id":1188793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188686-let-s-fix-the-disparates?p=1188786#post1188786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can think of three things that the Disparates do that the Traditions don't.<br /> <br /> 1) They are a <i>unique</i> combination of mismatched cultural groups. While the broad strokes run parallel to the Traditions, the devil is in the details. Different stories can be told with them, because the particular needs of the Crafts, and how they grind against each other, are not the same as those of the Traditions. Even in those instances when certain Crafts and Traditions are rough counterparts to one another. While the Wu Lung and Order of Hermes are both big into High Ritual Magick, their approaches to it, and their outlooks and attitudes, are far different, leading to different outcomes when those groups deal with other members of their respective sects.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2) As an adjunct to the above, the Disparates have a major difference from the Traditions: there are fewer White European groups in the Disparates. While the Traditions were multicultural, that sect had a large number of member groups that came from Europe or the West. Order of Hermes, Celestial Chorus, Verbana, Solificati, and multiple subsections of other Traditions. This European influence had major effects on how the Traditions were formed, developed, and operated. The Disparate Alliance, meanwhile, has a less prominent presence of White European culture, and a greater concentration of groups culled from non-White, non-European peoples and ideologies. Probably the single biggest Craft in the Alliance is the Bata'a, a group of Vodoun practitioners with a long history of problems with Whitey. For better or worse, this difference in race/culture representation DOES affect what kind of stories can be told with the Disparate Alliance.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3) Most importantly, the Disparate Alliance isn't just the Traditions. It's the Traditions AS FORMED IN MODERN DAY. The Council of Nine Mystic Traditions is a sect that is, by this point, Old. It's been around a while, and thus its members have figured out how to be in a combined sect about as well as they ever will. Inter-Tradition relations are hardly perfect, but the centuries these groups have worked together have made them familiar. They are comfortable in their place in the world, to a certain extent. The Traditions ARE.<br /> <br /> The Disparate Alliance, however, is New. It's untested, half-formed, and tenuous. The Disparate Alliance has a place in the game because it stands in contrast to the Traditions. It can go places the Traditions can't, because the latter is an established confederation. All this, while the two groups exist concurrently. You might be able to run a Traditions game where the sect is new...but you'd do it back in the Renaissance, which radically alters what kind of game you'd be playing. The Disparate Alliance allows one to run all the drama and story possibility that comes with a new, untested sect, while also having it play out in contemporary times.<br /> <br /> How do you think the idea of a First Cabal would play out in an era where modern telecommunications technology exists? How do you USE the fact that this new Mystic sect isn't the only major one in the Ascension War? Or hell, how much more interesting could it be for said Ascension War to have three big sides, rather than two? (Yes, the Nephandi and Marauders also exist, but they're smaller than the others, and have goals and methods that make them exceptions). How much more drama can arise when the technomancers in the Traditions are the only ones who could potentially be spies for a rival sect?</div> </div> </div> </div>And to add to this: the Disparate Alliance is the most representative of playing Mage in the 2010\u2019s. <br /> <br /> That in current socio-political climate has various minority groups becoming more empowered, more vocal on spreading the word, and overall increasing awareness and support for themselves. Mostly thanks to the changing values and communication technology of the time allowing these minority groups to be taken seriously and be heard. <br /> <br /> (Oh hai Black Panther being released recently as of this post and being a major cultural milestone)<br /> <br /> With a game where one of their core themes is \u201cfighting for what YOU believe in\u201d, seems pretty relevant and significant to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T02:21:35-08:00","id":1188806,"title":"","content":"I don't think we can &quot;fix&quot; the Disparate Alliance because fundamentally, I don't think it's broken. Sure, there's plenty of reasons people don't like it, but there's plenty of reasons people don't like... well lots of Mage.<br /> <br /> To me the biggest problem with the DA is something that's not fixable, because it's not something wrong with them, but the way they were introduced: they shouldn't have been presented as a major faction in M20's core book. If M20 simply had a chapter on Crafts, and the Alliance was part of a Future Fates box discussing one of the options for a Crafts focused game is its formation, I don't think anyone would be talking about needing to fix a thing. I think it would have been better received in general in that format.<br /> <br /> The introduction of an entire new faction to the game feels wrong in a giant omnibus book designed to run everything the game presented over the course of its original run. The Alliance was never part of that. Its formation isn't some strong point in the metaplot that needed addressing like the Nephandi infiltration of the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T08:02:30-08:00","id":1188872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That in current socio-political climate has various <b>minority groups becoming more empowered</b>, more vocal on spreading the word, and overall increasing awareness and support for themselves. Mostly thanks to the changing values and communication technology of the time allowing these minority groups to be taken seriously and be heard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps it's because I'm from South America, but I can't help but grin each time Bata'a are mentioned as a &quot;<i>minority</i>&quot;. You can't make two steps in my country without encountering someone who believes in Santeria or Umbanda. And not only poor people, you can find believers (that take it very seriously) from the lowest thug to politicians of every level, dictators, narcos, etc...by al means they should have a superb power base here.<br /> <br /> I remember it was stated in some book (don't remember where) that the Bata'a were suggested to take the Tenth Seat instead of the Holow Ones, but they weren't interested in joining the Tarditions, not even as a full fledged Tradition. They were OK on their own not-so-little corner of the world, thank you. That's the take I preffer on them.<br /> <br /> Heck. Santeria, Voudoon - they aren't different names for the same religion, they are different religions with the same root. Bata'a are already a coalition - more like the Celestial Chorus than the Children of Knowledge or the Templars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-23-2018, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T11:24:51-08:00","id":1188943,"title":"","content":"I think the way I'd run the Disparate Alliance is as a group that isn't interested in a war against anyone. They're another layer of the occult underground that is fixated on survival. <br /> The Nine Traditions are a big group that has been bumping shoulders and exchanging ideas for a long time. They've got their rivalries and their ideas have affected each other. They have a huge presence in Horizon and spend a lot of time in direct combat with the Technocracy. <br /> <br /> As the Technocracy intensified its pogrom against the crafts, it makes sense to me that at first, a lot of them would throw in with the Traditions as in Revised, but others who are more interested in survival than war would make a support network with just each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T13:10:29-08:00","id":1188973,"title":"","content":"For the Disparate Aliance, the looser the better.<br /> <br /> That's why I didn't like their strict legal system in BoS - I really can't see most of those persecuted isolationists not closing files on a member that was found guitly of a crime that matters more to others than to them. Allowing their execution &quot;for the beneffit of the whole&quot;.<br /> <br /> I would separate it in two groups: The cooperationists and the benefactors.<br /> <br /> The cooperationists are the heart of the Aliance. Groups that are able to work well with others but have beefs with the Traditions, that, coincidentally, are renown for their subtlety or their flexibility. Hollow Ones, Batini and stuff<br /> <br /> The benefactors are the outskirt. Groups that won't accept any outsider interference (for whatever reason), but may give a helping hand or accept it as a quid pro quo relationship. Like the Bata'a or the Templars.<br /> <br /> The cooperationists act like a loose but competent network of contacts and favors, they're the &quot;real&quot; Alliance, they have laws and stuff and sometimes join in multi-tradition cabals. Characterized by being as good or better at cooperation and non-intrusiveness as the Traditions these are the ones that have the big picture and organize stuff worldwide.<br /> <br /> The, politely called, benefactors, aren't really allied between themselves, but rather they are allied with at least one cooperationist faction. They don't have to obey anything from &quot;outsiders&quot; (esp. from heatens) - for most not having to obey the law of others was the reason to not join the Traditions in the first place - but rather have a relationship with factions that are sympathetic to them.<br /> <br /> This is easy to achieve thanks to the cooperationist inherent subtlety, multiculturalism or flexibility, they &quot;dress&quot; whatever the locals would find non-intrusive (you don't send a pagan witch to talk with the Templars, you seend someone from Avalon or a Hollow girl that fancies christian symbols). And they don't intrude. They don't demand them to obey laws, ask forgiveness or send help, but rather indulge in a favor network. <hr /><br /> But the greatest problem, one that wasn't adressed to my satisfaction, it's their role. Not-white mystics, multicultural, young, adapted to the 21 century -&gt; They're &quot;The Traditions but Better&quot;.<br /> <br /> I don't like that, the overlap it's way too much. Even if you like them, you have to ask yourself what's going to be the role of the Traditions (that were becoming multicultural themselves, as can be seen in the Book of the Traditions).<br /> <br /> The Disparate Alliance will trully end being the SJW group if they need to check-your-privilege the Traditions in order to have a <i>raison d'etre</i>. I couldn't ask for anything worse for such interesting (and, granted, needed) groups as the Ngoma, Bata'a, Taftanit, etc. These aren't &quot;<i>victims</i>&quot; that one should pitty, they are PROUD traditions that were willing to fight to the end rather than submitting.<br /> <br /> Moreso, it risks making the Traditions a bunch of white privilege european authoritarians that they don't need to be (and if they were, it was due to a flaw of the authors or the age, not a natural conclusion of their concept). Sadly, that seems the way things will go. Again, perhaps it's just me, but naming the new seat of the Council: &quot;<i>The Colony</i>&quot; has many negative connotations.<br /> <br /> I would instead take this approach: OK, they're the guys that refused to become all syncretist and join the Trads allied with the Trads that decided to leave because they couldn't stand the Hemretics (and other reasons). Then let's them be the (unwanted!) guardians of orthodoxy.<br /> <br /> The Traditions original goal was to preserve the old ways into the modern world, but they became too tied with each other and become...<i>different </i>(more hippy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> , but also more uniform). They failed to preserve the plurality of ways. <i>They failed to understood that no single way it's the only way</i>, because they crafted their own inner, secret, truth in the form of the hidden Paradigm: Were All God(s) in Disguise. So the Disparate are the (new) solution to the problem of Unity in Diversity. They persevere in the face of enemy and ally. They preserve the purity of Tradition. Even those that would bite their hand for offering it.<br /> <br /> On the side of the benefactors, you can play a True Traditionalist without being an Insufferable Bigot. If you want to play with a true Orthodox, the Traditions aren't for you because in the Traditions extremely divisive views are regarded as dangerous (you don't have to like each other, but you have to help each other). Incidentally, this it's the role that I use for the Crafts - the orthodox that won't compromise. Well, rest assured, the Disparate Alliance won't demand you to surrender your ways to be politically correct.<br /> <br /> On the side of the cooperativists, those that know or care about the agenda fight in order to allow *trully* different Paradigms to remain as strong as possible in an age where disolution (Nephandi), uniformity(Technocracy), and coalescence of ideas (Traditions) are the order of the day. To do so one must travel to hostile lands, not to bring peace but to bring the sword!. Expect nothing from the local mages, they don't even pretend to follow your laws. And do all of it knowing that something like the First Cabal isn't only impossible but undesirable because you don't seek compromise but to protect the other in it's otherness (if that makes any sense).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-23-2018, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T13:36:31-08:00","id":1188979,"title":"","content":"Now <i>that,</i> I can get behind. And like you, that's more or less how I've used the Crafts in the past: the uncompromising guardians of tradition. It's why I at one point floated the idea of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/441968-pillars-for-the-modern-crafts\">Pillars for the Modern Crafts</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T13:41:54-08:00","id":1188983,"title":"","content":"On record, I imagine that most Disparates would have Static Avatar essence in this interpretation. Not So Different indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T13:56:46-08:00","id":1188993,"title":"","content":"I have to say that I liked how Revised brought the Crafts under the wings of the Traditions. The Traditions grew from a few very discrete cultural groups to being huge umbrella groups fighting for everyone's right to preserve their beliefs and cultural practices.<br /> Portraying the Tradition Council as a bunch of white patriarchs really doesn't reflect any edition of Mage. Even the Order of Hermes, which was European dominated in Dark Ages Mage and Sorcerers Crusade games diversified quite a bit by the start of Mage 1st edition (1993) and became even more inclusive by Revised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":61,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","user":"Octavo","date":". 02-23-2018, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T13:57:53-08:00","id":1188994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188686-let-s-fix-the-disparates?p=1188983#post1188983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On record, I imagine that most Disparates would have Static Avatar essence in this interpretation. Not So Different indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not dynamic &quot;We must make our craft flourish as it had done in the times of old!&quot;<br /> <br /> or primordial &quot;Keep to the old ways, for they are truly the ways of wisedom&quot;<br /> <br /> or even questing &quot;We must strive to practice our craft, for if not us, then who?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T14:02:55-08:00","id":1188999,"title":"","content":"I tend to think of the Crafts being loosely aligned with the Primordial in the same way that the Technocracy is loosely aligned with the Static. That is, all four Essences appear in both alliances; but the Technocracy as a whole is about stability and order, and the Crafts as a whole are about the old ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-23-2018, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T14:05:09-08:00","id":1189001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188686-let-s-fix-the-disparates?p=1188994#post1188994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not dynamic &quot;We must make our craft flourish as it had done in the times of old!&quot;<br /> <br /> or primordial &quot;Keep to the old ways, for they are truly the ways of wisedom&quot;<br /> <br /> or even questing &quot;We must strive to practice our craft, for if not us, then who?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see Primordial and <i>maybe </i>Questing, but Dynamic seems like a stretch. How does returning to the old ways promote growth and change? How does it make you more open minded? Most Crafts, especially the more culturally isolated ones like the Kopa-Loei and the Knights Templar, have a paradigm just as rigid and a code of decorum just as rigid as anything the Technocracy has dreamed up.<br /> <br /> I mean, the whole reason they're not in the Traditions in the first place is that they're <i>not </i>willing to accept new ideas or change their perspectives! Sounds pretty static to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T14:08:42-08:00","id":1189002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188686-let-s-fix-the-disparates?p=1189001#post1189001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see Primordial and <i>maybe </i>Questing, but Dynamic seems like a stretch. How does returning to the old ways promote growth and change? How does it make you more open minded? Most Crafts, especially the more culturally isolated ones like the Kopa-Loei and the Knights Templar, have a paradigm just as rigid and a code of decorum just as rigid as anything the Technocracy has dreamed up.<br /> <br /> I mean, the whole reason they're not in the Traditions in the first place is that they're <i>not </i>willing to accept new ideas or change their perspectives! Sounds pretty static to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The templars aren't as catholic as they used to be. Also, they are now allowing women into their ranks. Change can be slow, but it's still change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T14:17:52-08:00","id":1189007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188686-let-s-fix-the-disparates?p=1189002#post1189002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The templars aren't as catholic as they used to be. Also, they are now allowing women into their ranks. Change can be slow, but it's still change.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the Technocracy is no longer an all male, ultra-colonialist organization. But they're still static.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T14:23:03-08:00","id":1189009,"title":"","content":"Again, the point with the Crafts isn't about change or the lack of it; it's about tradition and keeping the old ways. That's Primordial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T14:59:54-08:00","id":1189018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188686-let-s-fix-the-disparates?p=1189007#post1189007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Technocracy is no longer an all male, ultra-colonialist organization. But they're still static.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, individual technocrats can have all kinds of essences. Dynamic &quot;Technology can be used for the betterment of man kind!&quot;, Questing &quot;I must put an end to the poison that is the reality deviant&quot;, and even primordial &quot;The universe is a ticking clock, wound up at the big bang, and set to tick until it finally winds down. We must learn how it started to prevent its end.&quot;<br /> <br /> Similarly not all marauders are dynamic, and not all mages are questing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T15:02:24-08:00","id":1189021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188686-let-s-fix-the-disparates?p=1189018#post1189018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, individual technocrats can have all kinds of essences. Dynamic &quot;Technology can be used for the betterment of man kind!&quot;, Questing &quot;I must put an end to the poison that is the reality deviant&quot;, and even primordial &quot;The universe is a ticking clock, wound up at the big bang, and set to tick until it finally winds down. We must learn how it started to prevent its end.&quot;<br /> <br /> Similarly not all marauders are dynamic, and not all mages are questing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, Mages might characterize a faction as &quot;static&quot; or &quot;dynamic&quot;, but there's always variance at the individual level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T22:16:17-08:00","id":1189120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188686-let-s-fix-the-disparates?p=1188777#post1188777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's put it this way: why should we call foul on the Disparate Alliance being unlikely now, yet the Council of Nine Mystic Traditions is given a free pass?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because some of these are people who've spend 500 years saying &quot;NO I'M NOT JOINING A GROUP GO FUCK YOURSELVES!&quot;(the caps is important here). These groups seem to be odd choices as joiners(Well some of them). AND what they are joining doesn't seem to give them much?<br /> <br /> That and the Taftani were completely rewritten to the point that they aren't the same group.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also lets circle this back around, Why not have any of these groups join the council and make it &quot;more than 9&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T22:25:41-08:00","id":1189121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188686-let-s-fix-the-disparates?p=1188786#post1188786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 2) As an adjunct to the above, the Disparates have a major difference from the Traditions: there are fewer White European groups in the Disparates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only a PLURALITY of Disparates are White European based Groups. Because Groups can't have more than 9 members they couldn't have a solid 50 percent but If you look at the options for people to add to the list you could easily hit a European majority!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T01:25:28-08:00","id":1189152,"title":"","content":"In my game, the Disparate Alliance doesn\u00b4t exist. The individual Crafts exist, of course, as I love a lot of them (I am a GM, but if I was playing, I\u00b4d probably be a Ngoma or a Sister or a Taftani, or a Gnostic inspired &quot;We are all gods inside, strong burst of pain and pleasure just awaken the sleeping inner divinity, allowing it to make magic&quot; Orphan), but there isn\u00b4t an official Disparate Alliance in my game. What there is, is more eclectic alliances, in which individual Crafts collaborate with each other, or with the Traditions, depending on need, on a temporal or regional basis. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T04:38:26-08:00","id":1189191,"title":"","content":"I've been rethinking it, I think deep down my issue with the DA is that it removes options. For all the hamfisted pushing the various crafts into Traditions it allowed you to play a Wu Lung or a Templar etc along side Verbena or Hermetics and since the very beginning the option to have an orphan or Hollow One in your cabal was a thing. But by creating theirown faction suddenly having one of these in your Cabal is about as likely as a Technocrat","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T06:16:18-08:00","id":1189207,"title":"","content":"Except it doesn't. For one thing, the Craft-based Tradition factions still exist: if you want to play a Hermetic from House Solificati, you still have that option. Heck, if you want to play a House Solificati mage who is secretly a Child of Knowledge infiltrating the Traditions, you can do that, too \u2014 and that's a separate option from just playing a House Solificati alchemist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T06:26:19-08:00","id":1189209,"title":"","content":"I'm now imagining a scenario where a Hermtic solificati, a DA solificati and a pure craft solificati get drunk in a bar and start arguing about politics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T11:14:49-08:00","id":1189270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188686-let-s-fix-the-disparates?p=1189209#post1189209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm now imagining a scenario where a Hermtic solificati, a DA solificati and a pure craft solificati get drunk in a bar and start arguing about politics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You mean, like every Mage game ever? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T13:34:41-08:00","id":1191107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188686-let-s-fix-the-disparates?p=1188872#post1188872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps it's because I'm from South America, but I can't help but grin each time Bata'a are mentioned as a &quot;<i>minority</i>&quot;. You can't make two steps in my country without encountering someone who believes in Santeria or Umbanda. And not only poor people, you can find believers (that take it very seriously) from the lowest thug to politicians of every level, dictators, narcos, etc...by al means they should have a superb power base here.<br /> <br /> I remember it was stated in some book (don't remember where) that the Bata'a were suggested to take the Tenth Seat instead of the Holow Ones, but they weren't interested in joining the Tarditions, not even as a full fledged Tradition. They were OK on their own not-so-little corner of the world, thank you. That's the take I preffer on them.<br /> <br /> Heck. Santeria, Voudoon - they aren't different names for the same religion, they are different religions with the same root. Bata'a are already a coalition - more like the Celestial Chorus than the Children of Knowledge or the Templars.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, being from Brazil myself, I'd say that they're no a minority despite being big here in S.A. I'd say they are a minority BECAUSE they're from the S.A. And with the current attacks that umbanda and candombl\u00e9 practitionists have suffered in Brazil from radical christian groups, and even from &quot;donos do morro&quot; (Rio de Janeiro drug dealing slum lords), one could argue that they are, in fact, becoming more of a minority.<br /> <br /> I fully agree with your last paragraph, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6470-sardonis","name":"Sardonis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T15:39:50-08:00","id":1191150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sardonis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188686-let-s-fix-the-disparates?p=1191107#post1191107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Actually, being from Brazil myself, I'd say that they're no a minority despite being big here in S.A. I'd say they are a minority BECAUSE they're from the S.A</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting idea. I'm not sure if I understand or share your definition of &quot;minority&quot;. By that rule of three you and I are part of a &quot;minority&quot; in spite of me actually being white(ish) living in the capital of Argentina (where that's an advantage) and having a standard lifestile.<br /> <br /> I know native americans in my country are both less in number than half-blood and WAY more disadvantaged.<br /> <br /> That's a minority to me.<br /> <br /> My definition would be: A group of people that's less numerous and disadvantaged when compared to most people on their same situation. I wouldn't call the landlords of argentina a &quot;minority&quot; in that sense (albeit they are, by necesity, a minority - a whealty one) in spite of them being from S.A. Black people in my country, on the other hand, yeah, since the Yellow Fever (and the President Sarmiento) pretty much killed them all and now it's an odd racial trait that may bring you trouble.<br /> <br /> Hence I don't regard myself as part of a minority. Being on the losing side of Imperialism and wealth distribution a minority does not make.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> . And with the current attacks that umbanda and candombl\u00e9 practitionists have suffered in Brazil from radical christian groups, and even from &quot;donos do morro&quot; (Rio de Janeiro drug dealing slum lords), one could argue that they are, in fact, becoming more of a minority. </div> </div> </div>I don't know about that, but remember that Chavez and many of his antecessors had personal warlocks, and in my country there was a recent case of a kid being murdered in an umbanda ritual whose practicioners were fostered by a politician.<br /> <br /> If having influence from the bands of criminals to dictators, Union leaders and politicians isn't a powerbase I don't know what a powerbase is.<br /> <br /> Now, they aren't as powerful as Christians, but that's no shame given how powerful it's Christianity in your country (and S.A in general to a varying degree). I daresay that they would give the Technocracy itself a run for their money :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-02-2018, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T09:02:58-08:00","id":1192277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188686-let-s-fix-the-disparates?p=1191150#post1191150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's an interesting idea. I'm not sure if I understand or share your definition of &quot;minority&quot;. By that rule of three you and I are part of a &quot;minority&quot; in spite of me actually being white(ish) living in the capital of Argentina (where that's an advantage) and having a standard lifestile.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To begin with, I'll apologize in advance for probably breaking the quotes. I suck at editing them in any way, and odd things usually happen when I try to do it.<br /> <br /> Now, reading your comment, I believe I expressed myself poorly. I did not imply that I, myself, was part of a minority. I am a white heterosexual male of upper middle class. It's harder to be less of a minority than that. And I agree wholeheartedly with your definition of \u201cminority\u201d<br /> <br /> As an added bonus, my mother is a sporadic practitioner of candombl\u00e9 and an expert in African culture in Brazil, and has been to Haiti on work, and took part in voodoo rituals in the country.<br /> <br /> This is to say that, I mentioned being from Brazil to point out that I was in a privileged position to observe the current situation of Candombl\u00e9 and Umbanda practitioners. And, although they have a strong cultural presence (in particular in Bahia and Rio de Janeiro \u2013 I\u2019m from Rio myself), they have currently been recurrently persecuted by hate groups.<br /> <br /> Apart from some unusual cases (like that of Papa Doc in Haiti), and even some funny ones (like the former mayor of Rio, who would go to a M\u00e3e de Santo every year to ask for cleat weather during New Year\u2019s Eve) those groups have been persecuted due to the double \u201ccrimes\u201d of mostly including black people and not being Christian.<br /> <br /> Do I believe that making a Hougan or Pai de Santo character with strong political connections would be awesome? YES. (Papa Midnite comes to mind, in fact) Are they, for the most part, representatives of a minority? Sadly, also yes, and more so now than in the recent past, in Brazil at least.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6470-sardonis","name":"Sardonis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}